# Schema V2 Activation-Artifact Finalization Package V1

## Purpose

This package contains review candidates for the two remaining Schema V2
activation artifacts authorized by Decision 0061:

1. the finalized V1/V2 version-dispatch policy; and
2. the finalized successor text to historical Decision 0019.

It also binds the separately human-approved Schema V2 hash-contract active
form, which requires no further transformation.

## Exact dispatch candidate

Source SHA-256:

`5a91a9938af7029edff6b91b8b624b2f0712680d49fad3abd1be29e649944bce`

Active-form review-candidate SHA-256:

`67a96c3eda8de95fa6c55342d5d33ea725e16cea8af21fcb4f3b8945b9d4eeee`

The only permitted JSON change is:

`$.status`

from `REVIEW_CANDIDATE_NOT_ACTIVE` to
`ACTIVE_UPON_EXPLICIT_SCHEMA_V2_ACTIVATION_DECISION`.

Future active path:

`config/protocol_specification_schema_version_dispatch.v1.json`

That path is not created by this package.

## Exact Decision-0019 successor candidate

Source SHA-256:

`8665163eb5d4f7a8718ba3ed2d3973ba928fea85789c23696599a2d6ea02bbb3`

Active-form review-candidate SHA-256:

`a96f9d8b6811a9f9170a18de9ff8be6f80a3704b9e6a13c59fbb88e423bec3bb`

Exactly three transformations are permitted: title finalization, status
finalization, and replacement of the candidate-only activation-condition
paragraph.

All other source text must remain byte-preserved.

Historical Decision 0019 itself remains immutable.

## Approved V2 hash-contract active form

SHA-256:

`37f035bb617f5598a0e368ba3b60b4bf1e69e4e69ce2f1053d71c0fcc96619e9`

This package does not transform, install, or activate it.

## Required independent human review

AF01 through AF10 must be reviewed independently before any later Schema V2
activation decision.

## Explicit non-effects

This package does not create or install the active V2 hash contract, create or
install the active version-dispatch policy, activate Schema V2, adopt the
Decision-0019 successor, define positive V4-to-V2 mapping, create curl.json,
authorize analyzer implementation/execution, authorize baseline execution, or
authorize repair.
